Version 0.6 (2026-05-21)

- Fix tuplet bracket placement for MIDI-recorded files: notes whose tuplet ratio
  is inferred from duration (actualNotes=0 in the Encore file) are now correctly
  recognized by the look-ahead logic that decides when to close a tuplet group.
  Previously the look-ahead checked only the stored actualNotes field, causing
  premature tuplet-stop markers that left the next note as an orphaned
  tuplet-start, which MuseScore imported as an incomplete tuplet.
- Fix gap rest splitting: when the remaining space at the end of a voice is a
  non-standard duration (not representable as a single note type), write it as
  multiple standard-duration rests instead of a single typeless rest. A typeless
  rest caused MuseScore's TDuration to round to the nearest standard value and
  place the wrong number of ticks, producing "Incomplete measure" corruption.
- Fix chord note tuplet detection: notes whose actualNotes is 0 in the file now
  correctly detect their tuplet ratio via the note duration and face value, so
  the time-modification element is written when the surrounding context has
  proper tuplet brackets.
- Improve MIDI-recorded large orchestral file compatibility (tested against
  atraing.enc, a 31-staff MIDI-recorded score).
- Add key signature tracking for correct pitch spelling when key changes occur.
- Support instrument name recovery from formula positions for v0xC4 files.
- Support staff visibility flag.

Version 0.5 (2018-09-29)

- support words (staff text)
- support tempo marker
- support wedge
- support tie
- support slur
- support fermata
- add alternative dump format

Version 0.4.2 (2018-08-19)

- MusicXML writer refactoring (no functional changes)

Version 0.4.1 (2018-08-18)

- MusicXML writer refactoring (no functional changes)

Version 0.4 (2018-08-12)

- support multi-staff parts
- handle files without TKxx blocks
- ignore measure elements type lyric and unknown type 10 and 11
- support SCO5 files
- support SCOW files without TKxx blocks

Version 0.3 (2018-08-02)

- support grace notes
- support chords
- support multiple voices
- change divisions from 480 to 240

Version 0.2 (2018-07-20)

- Support repeats, including alternative endings and segno and coda.
- Support different clefs.
- Improve accidental handling.
- Support multi-line header text.
- Support multiple single staff / single voice parts.

Version 0.1 (2018-06-06)

Proof of concept. Only files with a single part using one voice are supported.
